meta {
  name: logout
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "refresh_token": "{{refreshToken}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Revokes the refresh family. The access token keeps working until it
  expires, which is not a bug: access tokens are stateless by design
  (ADR-0007), and that is why they are short-lived. This is why the users/
  folder still works after this request runs.

  The converse is worth knowing: refreshToken now points at a revoked
  family. Re-running refresh on its own answers 401 and is recorded as a
  replay, bumping refresh_reuse_detected_total — a real security signal
  raised by an idle click. Run login again first.
}
